{"parse": {"title": "Brutus", "pageid": 646156, "revid": 15364604, "redirects": [], "wikitext": {"*": "{{Otheruses|the standard boss|the harder variant|Demonic Brutus}}\n{{Instance}}\n{{HasStrategy}}\n{{HasTask|Cows}}\n{{Infobox Monster\n|name = Brutus\n|image = [[File:Brutus.png|280px]]\n|release = [[25 February]] [[2026]]\n|update = Cow Boss is Out Today!\n|members = No\n|combat = 30\n|size = 3\n|examine = Doesn't skip leg day.\n|xpbonus = +100.0\n|flatarmour = 0\n|max hit = 3 (melee), 19 (special)\n|aggressive = Yes\n|poisonous = No\n|attack style = [[Crush]]\n|attack speed = 5\n|respawn = 36 ticks (21.6s), or 13 ticks (7.8s) upon ringing [[cowbell amulet]]\n|slayxp = 116\n|cat = Cows\n|assignedby = turael,spria\n|hitpoints = 58\n|att = 12\n|str = 25\n|def = 10\n|mage = 8\n|range = 1\n|attbns = 0\n|strbns = 0\n|amagic = 0\n|mbns = 0\n|arange = 0\n|rngbns = 0\n|dstab = -7\n|dslash = -7\n|dcrush = -7\n|dmagic = -3\n|dlight = -7\n|dstandard = -7\n|dheavy = -7\n|elementalweaknesstype = Earth\n|elementalweaknesspercent = 25\n|poisonresistance = 0\n|venomresistance = 0\n|immunecannon = Yes\n|immuneburn = No\n|id = 15626,15627\n|leagueRegion = Misthalin\n}}\n'''Brutus''' is a low-level [[free-to-play]] [[boss]] located in the [[Lumbridge cow field]], whom players defeat as part of the quest [[The Ides of Milk]], and can be fought after completion of the quest as a boss encounter. During the quest, he cannot kill the player with standard attacks (though his charge and stomp attacks can still kill) and does not drop anything.\n\nThe boss is designed to be accessible for low-level players. Unlike [[Scurrius]], which requires some investment before fighting him, Brutus can be reasonably fought almost immediately after starting the game and teaches players a few aspects of bossing, such as dodging telegraphed attacks. Brutus also gives double the normal rate of combat experience.\n\nBrutus is an excellent source for [[Clue scroll (beginner)|beginner clue scrolls]], especially for higher level players who can kill the boss quickly. He also drops [[Clue scroll (easy)|easy clue scrolls]] at a lower rate.\n\nUpon completion of [[Desert Treasure II - The Fallen Empire]], a stronger version of Brutus, known as [[Demonic Brutus]], can be fought by feeding him an [[abyssal potato]]; one potato permits only one attempt, but these are readily available from the [[Growth (The Scar)|growth]] found in [[the Scar]].\n\n==Location==\n{{LocTableHead}}\n{{LocLine\n|name = Brutus\n|location = [[Lumbridge cow field]]\n|levels = 30\n|members = No\n|x:3263,y:3297\n|mtype = pin\n|leagueRegion = Misthalin\n}}\n{{LocTableBottom}}\n\n==Strategy==\n{{Main|Brutus/Strategies}}\n\nAside from a basic melee attack that can be negated through the use of the [[Protect from Melee]] prayer, Brutus uses two special attacks, both of which give players a few [[ticks]] to move out of the way.\n\nThe two attacks are as follows; \n{| class=\"wikitable\"\n|+\n!Attack\n!Text\n!Effect\n!Tiles\n!Strat\n|-\n|Charge\n|*growls*\n|15-19\n|Dash forward 4 Tiles\n|Move to the side of his charge to avoid. He will face the way he charges\n|-\n|Stomp\n|*snort*\n|15-19\n|3-6 tiles in front of him\n|Stomps the corner tiles or the 3 directly in front of him. Normally stomps between 1 and 3 times. Move backwards 1 tile to avoid.\n|}\nAdditionally, Brutus cannot be [[Flinching|flinched]], but he can be temporarily [[safespot]]ted on nearby scenery objects (such as plants or with the nearby warning sign or troughs). After a short while of being safespotted, Brutus can either charge towards the player through obstacles or move around them to reach the player. However, if you stand between both food troughs far south (the square touching the fence), you can safespot Brutus using range or magic.\n\n==Drops==\n{{Listen\n|filename = Unique drop sound effect.ogg\n|title = Unique drop [[sound effect]]\n|desc = The sound that plays when receiving a unique drop.\n|align = right\n}}\n{{DropLogProject|kills=815419}}\n\n{{Average drop value|mob=Brutus#Members}}\n\n===100%===\n{{DropsTableHead}}\n{{DropsLine|name=Bull bones|quantity=1|rarity=Always|gemw=no}}\n{{DropsLine|name=Raw t-bone steak|quantity=1|rarity=Always}}\n{{DropsTableBottom}}\n\n===Pre-roll===\n''The mooleta's rarity is the same on both members' and free-to-play worlds.''\n{{DropsTableHead}}\n{{DropsLine|name=Mooleta|quantity=1|rarity=5/150|gemw=no}}\n{{DropsLine|name=Bottomless milk bucket (empty)|quantity=1|rarity=4/150|namenotes={{(m)}}|gemw=no}}\n{{DropsLine|name=Cow slippers|quantity=1|rarity=1/150|namenotes={{(m)}}|gemw=yes}}\n{{DropsTableBottom}}\n\n===Armour===\n{{DropsTableHead}}\n{{DropsLine|name=Iron full helm|quantity=1|rarity=2/81}}\n{{DropsLine|name=Iron platebody|quantity=1|rarity=2/81}}\n{{DropsLine|name=Iron platelegs|quantity=1|rarity=1/81}}\n{{DropsLine|name=Iron plateskirt|quantity=1|rarity=1/81}}\n{{DropsTableBottom}}\n\n===Runes and ammunition===\n{{DropsTableHead}}\n{{DropsLine|name=Iron arrow|quantity=14|rarity=10/81}}\n{{DropsLine|name=Air rune|quantity=29|rarity=10/81}}\n{{DropsLine|name=Mind rune|quantity=18|rarity=8/81}}\n{{DropsLine|name=Chaos rune|quantity=12|rarity=2/81}}\n{{DropsTableBottom}}\n\n===Seeds===\n{{DropsTableHead}}\n{{DropsLine|name=Potato seed|quantity=3|rarity=10/81|namenotes={{(m)}}}}\n{{DropsLine|name=Acorn|quantity=2|rarity=5/81|namenotes={{(m)}}}}\n{{DropsTableBottom}}\n\n===Resources===\n{{DropsTableHead}}\n{{DropsLine|name=Raw t-bone steak|quantity=3 (noted)|rarity=10/81|namenotes={{(m)}}}}\n{{DropsLine|name=Cowhide|quantity=1|rarity=10/81}}\n{{DropsLine|name=Oak logs|quantity=2|rarity=5/81}}\n{{DropsLine|name=Logs|quantity=2|rarity=5/81}}\n{{DropsTableBottom}}\n\n===Other===\n''Seeds and noted steaks are replaced by coins on free-to-play worlds.''\n{{DropsTableHead}}\n{{DropsLine|name=Coins|quantity=60-80|rarity=15/81|namenotes={{(f)}}}}\n{{DropsLine|name=Coins|quantity=80-100|rarity=5/81|namenotes={{(f)}}}}\n{{DropsLine|name=Coins|quantity=100-120|rarity=5/81|namenotes={{(f)}}}}\n{{DropsTableBottom}}\n\n===Tertiary===\n{{DropsTableHead}}\n{{DropsLineClue|type=beginner|rarity=1/15}}\n{{DropsLineClue|type=easy|quantity=1|rarity=1/40|f2p=yes}}\n{{DropsLine|name=Beef|quantity=1|rarity=1/1000|gemw=no|namenotes={{(m)}}}}\n{{DropsTableBottom}}\n\n==Collection log==\nBrutus has 4 [[collection log]] items.\n{{Sync}}\n{{Collection log list|category=Brutus}}\n\n==Combat Achievements==\n{{Combat Achievements list|Brutus}}\n\n==Dialogue==\n{{Hastranscript|npc}}\n\n==Changes==\n{{Subject changes header}}\n{{Subject changes\n|date = 23 April 2026\n|update = Leagues VI Changes\n|change = The [[Combat Achievements]] interface now shows the correct number of completed tasks for Brutus.\n}}\n{{Subject changes\n|date = 4 March 2026\n|update = Cow Boss and Skill Guide & Level-Up Changes\n|change =\n* Adjusted Brutus’s soft anti-safespot mechanics so that he now uses his stomp special attack if he’s safespotted while the player is only one tile away.\n* Added a \"Yes and don't ask again\" option when releasing Brutus from his pen.\n}}\n{{Subject changes footer}}\n\n==Gallery==\n<gallery mode=\"packed\" heights=\"180\" style=\"text-align:left\">\nBrutus concept art.png|Concept of Brutus, by [[Mod Jerv]].\nWinter_Summit_2026_-_Overview_(7).png|Concept art of the boss's rewards, by [[Mod Skylark]].\n</gallery>\n\n==Trivia==\n*Brutus is the only free-to-play boss that has [[Combat Achievement]] tasks in the hard and elite tier.\n*The acorn drop is a reference to [[Mod Acorn]] who developed the boss alongside [[Mod Arcane]] during [[Game Jam VII]].\n*Like [[Cassius]] and the Ides of Milk quest, Brutus' name is a reference to the Assassination of Julius Caesar, specifically to Marcus Junius Brutus, one of the most prominent and well-known conspirators in the plot.\n*Using an item on Brutus prompts the message {{mes|Brutus doesn't want that.}} as opposed to the usual {{mes|Nothing interesting happens.}}\n*Using an empty bucket on Brutus prompts the message {{mes|You do not want to do that.}}\n*Killing Brutus or his demonic variant while the player is wearing [[Cow31337Killer]]'s outfit ([[rune boots]], [[rune platebody]], [[rune plateskirt]], [[Klank's gauntlets]], [[Dharok's helm]], and [[Dharok's greataxe]]) prompts the message {{mes|You are but an imitation of a true legend.}}\n*As of 27 February 2026, Brutus and his demonic variant had killed players a total of 153,350 times, of which 35 of those were hardcore ironmen. The reclaim cost from these deaths also totaled 44,200,000,000 coins.{{CiteTwitter|url=https://twitter.com/OldSchoolRS/status/2027111781286429109|date=26 February 2026|quote=Mess with the bull? You get the horns!<br />Brutus' easy & hard mode has killed players 153,550 times & 35 of those players were hardcore ironmen so far. This has cost players 44.2B 🥛|author=OldSchoolRS|archiveurl=https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/27964123|archivedate=17 June 2026}}\n*The [[scoreboard (Brutus)|scoreboard]] next to Brutus' pen has morse code on it that translates to [https://simpsonswiki.com/wiki/Malk \"MALK\"].{{sic}}\n\n==References==\n{{reflist}}\n\n{{Brutus}}\n{{Bosses}}"}}, "fetchedAt": "2026-10-06T04:21:49.420053+00:00", "dropHtml": "<table class=\"wikitable sortable filterable item-drops autosort=4,a\" style=\"text-align:center\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th style=\"border-right: none;\" class=\"drops-img-header drop-disp-btn unsortable\" title=\"Sort items by category, rarity and name.\"></th>\n<th style=\"border-left: none;\" class=\"item-col\">Item</th>\n<th data-sort-type=\"number\">Quantity</th>\n<th>Rarity</th>\n<th class=\"ge-column\" data-sort-type=\"number\">Price</th>\n<th class=\"alch-column\" data-sort-type=\"number\">High Alch</th>\n</tr>\n\n<tr style=\"text-align:center\"><td class=\"inventory-image\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/w/Bull_bones\" title=\"Bull bones\"><img alt=\"Bull bones.png: Brutus drops Bull bones with rarity Always in quantity 1\" src=\"